    "decisions": {
      "D-210": "UI term for students is 'murid' (Meja/Kursi Murid).",
      "D-217": "School inventory (O4) is in scope.",
      "D-219": "No BOS/RKAS reports; funding sources do not name BOS (see also D-025).",
      "D-305": "Catalog copied from usulan-01 for one Tim Validasi review.",
      "D-306": "An inventory item belongs to the school and sits in a room; the wali kelas edits condition and count for their own room. This list is the item picker for both views.",
      "D-367": "Curated with SIGRAK names, keys, and codes."
    },
    "conventions": [
      "Keys are English snake_case and never change once seeded; labels and other text shown to users are Indonesian.",
      "Codes follow SIGRAK-KAT-<AREA>-NN for the main items of a file and SIGRAK-KAT-<AREA>-<LIST>-NN for its secondary lists (see README.md). Codes are stable: a retired item keeps its code, and new items take the next free number.",
      "No identifier from the legacy app is carried over. Where a decision keeps an old label for reference (D-305), it sits in legacy_label and is never shown in the UI.",
      "review_notes are Indonesian notes for Tim Validasi SIGRAK; they are not shown to teachers.",
      "items is the suggested item list for class_inventory_items (docs/final/data-model.md); a school can type any other item through 'other'.",
      "conditions and funding_sources are proposals (origin = proposed): the legacy app had three options each, but their text was not readable in the source.",
      "conditions follow the usual terms of the regional asset register (Baik, Rusak ringan, Rusak berat)."
    ]
  },
